IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgk-div8-register`

-- Tests for ss 134 to 138. Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the assertion.

§ `Section 134`

-- (1): (a) a series of debentures: the four particulars of a s 131(5) statement; (b) any other charge: (i) date of creation (or of the acquisition), (ii) amount secured, (iii) description of the property, (iv) name of the person entitled.
#ASSERT count (`s 134(1) the particulars the Registrar must enter in the register` `s 134(1)(a) a charge to the benefit of which the holders of a series of debentures are entitled`) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT elem "the total amount secured by the whole series" (`s 134(1) the particulars the Registrar must enter in the register` `s 134(1)(a) a charge to the benefit of which the holders of a series of debentures are entitled`)
#ASSERT elem "the names of the trustee (if any) for the debenture holders" (`s 134(1) the particulars the Registrar must enter in the register` `s 134(1)(a) a charge to the benefit of which the holders of a series of debentures are entitled`)
#ASSERT count (`s 134(1) the particulars the Registrar must enter in the register` `s 134(1)(b) any other charge created by the company`) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT elem "the date of the creation of the charge" (`s 134(1) the particulars the Registrar must enter in the register` `s 134(1)(b) any other charge created by the company`)
#ASSERT NOT (elem "the date of the acquisition of the property" (`s 134(1) the particulars the Registrar must enter in the register` `s 134(1)(b) any other charge created by the company`))
#ASSERT count (`s 134(1) the particulars the Registrar must enter in the register` `s 134(1)(b) any other charge existing on property acquired by the company`) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT elem "the date of the acquisition of the property" (`s 134(1) the particulars the Registrar must enter in the register` `s 134(1)(b) any other charge existing on property acquired by the company`)
#ASSERT elem "the name of the person entitled to the charge" (`s 134(1) the particulars the Registrar must enter in the register` `s 134(1)(b) any other charge existing on property acquired by the company`)
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 134(1) the Registrar must enter the particulars of the charge in the register` 7 AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 134(1) the Registrar must enter the particulars of the charge in the register` 45 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 134(1) enter the particulars of the charge in the register` AT 3

-- late: the act is done on day 400, past the 7 days the input is, so BREACH
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 134(1) the Registrar must enter the particulars of the charge in the register` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 134(1) enter the particulars of the charge in the register` AT 400

-- (2): "the notice is conclusive evidence"; (3): "the certificate is conclusive evidence"; the certificate issues "Upon the application of the company and payment of the prescribed fee".
#ASSERT `s 134(2) the notice is conclusive evidence that the requirements as to registration have been complied with` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 134(2) the notice is conclusive evidence that the requirements as to registration have been complied with` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 134(3) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 134(3) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 134(3) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 134(3) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements as to registration have been complied with` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 134(3) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements as to registration have been complied with` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 134(2) the Registrar must issue to the company a notice of the registration of a charge` 7 AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 134(2) the Registrar must issue to the company a notice of the registration of a charge` 45 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 134(2) issue to the company a notice of the registration of the charge` AT 2

-- late: the act is done on day 400, past the 7 days the input is, so BREACH
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 134(2) the Registrar must issue to the company a notice of the registration of a charge` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 134(2) issue to the company a notice of the registration of the charge` AT 400

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 134(3) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` 7 AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 134(3) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` 45 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 134(3) issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` AT 2

-- late: the act is done on day 400, past the 7 days the input is, so BREACH
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 134(3) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 134(3) issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` AT 400

§ `Section 135`

-- (1) and (2): arguments: a series debenture or certificate issued by the company?, secured by a registered charge?, issued before the charge was registered?
#ASSERT `s 135(1) the company must cause a copy of the notice of registration, or a statement of the registration and its date, to be endorsed on the debenture or certificate` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 135(1) the company must cause a copy of the notice of registration, or a statement of the registration and its date, to be endorsed on the debenture or certificate` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- (2): issued before the charge was registered
#ASSERT `s 135(1) the company must cause a copy of the notice of registration, or a statement of the registration and its date, to be endorsed on the debenture or certificate` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING    -- not a series debenture or certificate
#ASSERT `s 135(1) the company must cause a copy of the notice of registration, or a statement of the registration and its date, to be endorsed on the debenture or certificate` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING    -- not secured by a registered charge
-- (3): knowingly and wilfully authorising or permitting delivery of an unendorsed instrument; fine not exceeding $2,000.
#ASSERT `s 135(3) the person is guilty of the offence of authorising or permitting the delivery of an unendorsed debenture or certificate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 135(3) the person is guilty of the offence of authorising or permitting the delivery of an unendorsed debenture or certificate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- not "knowingly and wilfully" (split site (i))
#ASSERT `s 135(3) the person is guilty of the offence of authorising or permitting the delivery of an unendorsed debenture or certificate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- endorsed as required
#ASSERT `s 135(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 135(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 135(1) the company must cause the endorsement to be made` "Acme Ltd" AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 135(1) the company must cause the endorsement to be made` "Acme Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Ltd" DOES `s 135(1) endorse on the debenture or certificate of debenture stock a copy of the notice of registration or a statement of the registration` AT 4
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 135(3) a person must not knowingly and wilfully authorise or permit the delivery of an unendorsed debenture or certificate` "A. Tan" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "A. Tan" DOES `s 135(3) authorise or permit the delivery of a debenture or certificate of debenture stock not endorsed as section 135 requires` AT 5
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 135(3) a person must not knowingly and wilfully authorise or permit the delivery of an unendorsed debenture or certificate` "A. Tan" AT 0 WITH

§ `Section 136`

#ASSERT `s 136(1) the company may lodge with the Registrar a statement of satisfaction or release` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE       -- (a) paid or satisfied in whole or in part
#ASSERT `s 136(1) the company may lodge with the Registrar a statement of satisfaction or release` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE       -- (b) released or ceased to form part
#ASSERT `s 136(1) the company may lodge with the Registrar a statement of satisfaction or release` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- "Where" neither (fork F-K7)
#ASSERT `s 136(1) the Registrar must enter the particulars of the statement in the register` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 136(1) the Registrar must enter the particulars of the statement in the register` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 136(2) the statement of satisfaction or release is endorsed as the subsection requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 136(2) the statement of satisfaction or release is endorsed as the subsection requires` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 136(2) the chargee's statement constitutes sufficient evidence of the payment, satisfaction, release or ceasing` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 136(2) the chargee's statement constitutes sufficient evidence of the payment, satisfaction, release or ceasing` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 136(1) the Registrar must enter the particulars of the statement in the register` 7 AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 136(1) the Registrar must enter the particulars of the statement in the register` 45 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 136(1) enter the particulars of the statement of satisfaction or release in the register` AT 7

-- late: the act is done on day 400, past the 7 days the input is, so BREACH
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 136(1) the Registrar must enter the particulars of the statement in the register` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 136(1) enter the particulars of the statement of satisfaction or release in the register` AT 400

§ `Section 137`

-- Arguments: the person is the company?, a person interested?, an omission or mis-statement of the kind described?
#ASSERT `s 137 the person may apply to the Court for the extension of time or the rectification` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137 the person may apply to the Court for the extension of time or the rectification` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137 the person may apply to the Court for the extension of time or the rectification` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137 the person may apply to the Court for the extension of time or the rectification` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: application made?, accidental or inadvertence or other sufficient cause?, not prejudicial?, just and equitable?
#ASSERT `s 137 the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137 the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137 the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137 the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING    -- no ground
#ASSERT `s 137 the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING    -- no application
#ASSERT `s 137 the Court may make the relief subject to a term that it is without prejudice to liability already incurred in respect of the default` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137 the Court may make the relief subject to a term that it is without prejudice to liability already incurred in respect of the default` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 138(1) and (1A)`

#ASSERT `s 138(1) the company must keep the instrument creating the charge, or a copy, at its registered office` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 138(1) the company must keep the instrument creating the charge, or a copy, at its registered office` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- "for as long as the charge ... remains in force": it no longer does
#ASSERT `s 138(1) the company must keep the instrument creating the charge, or a copy, at its registered office` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING         -- a charge not requiring registration
#ASSERT `s 138(1) the company's keeping satisfies the subsection` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 138(1) the company's keeping satisfies the subsection` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- a series: a copy of one debenture of the series is sufficient
#ASSERT `s 138(1) the company's keeping satisfies the subsection` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 138(1) the company's keeping satisfies the subsection` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE    -- a copy of one debenture is enough only for a series
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 138(1) the company must keep the instrument or a copy at its registered office` "Acme Ltd" AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 138(1) the company must keep the instrument or a copy at its registered office` "Acme Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Ltd" DOES `s 138(1) keep the instrument creating the charge, or a copy, at the registered office` AT 10
-- The prohibition for the life of a charge in force for 365 days: ceasing to keep the instrument on day 100 is a breach; on day 366 it is outside the charge's life.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 138(1) the company must not cease to keep the instrument or a copy at its registered office while the charge remains in force` "Acme Ltd" 365 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Ltd" DOES `s 138(1) cease to keep the instrument creating the charge, or a copy, at the registered office while the charge remains in force` AT 100
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 138(1) the company must not cease to keep the instrument or a copy at its registered office while the charge remains in force` "Acme Ltd" 365 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Ltd" DOES `s 138(1) cease to keep the instrument creating the charge, or a copy, at the registered office while the charge remains in force` AT 366
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 138(1) the company must not cease to keep the instrument or a copy at its registered office while the charge remains in force` "Acme Ltd" 365 AT 0 WITH

#ASSERT `s 138(1A)(a) the instrument or copy is deemed to form part of the records required to be kept under section 199(1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 138(1A)(a) the instrument or copy is deemed to form part of the records required to be kept under section 199(1)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1A)(b): 5 years after (i) the debt paid in whole; (ii) the property released; (iii) both: the later date.
#ASSERT `s 138(1A)(b) the last day of the period of 5 years for which the instrument must be retained` TRUE (Date 15 3 2021) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 138(1A)(b) the last day of the period of 5 years for which the instrument must be retained` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 20 8 2022) EQUALS JUST (Date 20 8 2027)
#ASSERT `s 138(1A)(b) the last day of the period of 5 years for which the instrument must be retained` TRUE (Date 15 3 2021) TRUE (Date 20 8 2022) EQUALS JUST (Date 20 8 2027)     -- the later of the dates: the release
#ASSERT `s 138(1A)(b) the last day of the period of 5 years for which the instrument must be retained` TRUE (Date 1 12 2023) TRUE (Date 2 1 2021) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 12 2028)     -- the later of the dates: the payment
#ASSERT `s 138(1A)(b) the last day of the period of 5 years for which the instrument must be retained` TRUE (Date 29 2 2024) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2029)    -- 5 years after 29 February 2024: no 29 February in 2029, so 28 February (convention P4)
#ASSERT `s 138(1A)(b) the last day of the period of 5 years for which the instrument must be retained` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING    -- neither event has occurred
#ASSERT `s 138(1A)(b) the instrument must still be retained on the day` (Date 15 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- the last day
#ASSERT `s 138(1A)(b) the instrument must still be retained on the day` (Date 16 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- the day after
#ASSERT `s 138(1A)(b) the instrument must still be retained on the day` (Date 16 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 138(2) to (4)`

#ASSERT count (`s 138(2) the particulars the company must give of each charge in its register of charges` FALSE) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT elem "the names of the persons entitled to the charge" (`s 138(2) the particulars the company must give of each charge in its register of charges` FALSE)
#ASSERT count (`s 138(2) the particulars the company must give of each charge in its register of charges` TRUE) EQUALS 2                -- "except in the case of securities to bearer"
#ASSERT NOT (elem "the names of the persons entitled to the charge" (`s 138(2) the particulars the company must give of each charge in its register of charges` TRUE))
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 138(2) the company must keep a register of charges at its registered office` "Acme Ltd" AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 138(2) the company must keep a register of charges at its registered office` "Acme Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Ltd" DOES `s 138(2) keep a register of charges at the registered office` AT 2

-- (3): any creditor or member without fee; any other person may inspect the register for a fee not exceeding $2.
#ASSERT `s 138(3) the item must be open to the person's inspection` `s 138(3) a creditor of the company` `s 138(3) the instruments or copies kept under section 138` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 138(3) the item must be open to the person's inspection` `s 138(3) a member of the company` `s 138(3) the register of charges` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 138(3) the item must be open to the person's inspection` `s 138(3) any other person` `s 138(3) the register of charges` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 138(3) the item must be open to the person's inspection` `s 138(3) any other person` `s 138(3) the instruments or copies kept under section 138` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 138(3) the most the company may charge for one inspection` `s 138(3) a creditor of the company` `s 138(3) the register of charges` EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 138(3) the most the company may charge for one inspection` `s 138(3) a member of the company` `s 138(3) the instruments or copies kept under section 138` EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 138(3) the most the company may charge for one inspection` `s 138(3) any other person` `s 138(3) the register of charges` EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `s 138(3) the most the company may charge for one inspection` `s 138(3) any other person` `s 138(3) the instruments or copies kept under section 138` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 138(3) the fee the company has fixed is within the limit` `s 138(3) any other person` `s 138(3) the register of charges` 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE       -- "not exceeding $2": $2 is within
#ASSERT `s 138(3) the fee the company has fixed is within the limit` `s 138(3) any other person` `s 138(3) the register of charges` 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- $3 is not
#ASSERT `s 138(3) the fee the company has fixed is within the limit` `s 138(3) a creditor of the company` `s 138(3) the register of charges` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 138(3) the fee the company has fixed is within the limit` `s 138(3) a member of the company` `s 138(3) the register of charges` 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- "without fee"
#ASSERT `s 138(3) the fee the company has fixed is within the limit` `s 138(3) any other person` `s 138(3) the instruments or copies kept under section 138` 1 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3A): a copy within 3 days of the application, for not more than $1 a page or part of a page.
#ASSERT `s 138(3A) the person may be furnished with a copy of the instrument or debenture` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 138(3A) the person may be furnished with a copy of the instrument or debenture` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING        -- fee not paid (fork F-K15)
#ASSERT `s 138(3A) the person may be furnished with a copy of the instrument or debenture` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING        -- no application
#ASSERT `s 138(3A) the last day for furnishing the copy` (Date 10 5 2026) EQUALS Date 13 5 2026                            -- 3 days after 10 May
#ASSERT `s 138(3A) the last day for furnishing the copy` (Date 30 12 2026) EQUALS Date 2 1 2027                            -- across the year end
#ASSERT `s 138(3A) the most the company may charge for the copy, in Singapore dollars` 7 EQUALS 7                          -- $1 for every page or part
#ASSERT `s 138(3A) the most the company may charge for the copy, in Singapore dollars` 0 EQUALS 0
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 138(3A) the company must furnish the copy within 3 days of the application` "Acme Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Ltd" DOES `s 138(3A) furnish the person with a copy of an instrument or debenture kept under section 138` AT 3
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 138(3A) the company must furnish the copy within 3 days of the application` "Acme Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Ltd" DOES `s 138(3A) furnish the person with a copy of an instrument or debenture kept under section 138` AT 4
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 138(3A) the company must furnish the copy within 3 days of the application` "Acme Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 4)
-- (4): the offence: fine not exceeding $2,000 and a default penalty.
#ASSERT `s 138(4) the person is guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 138` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 138(4) the person is guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 138` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 138(4) the person is guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 138` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 138(4) the person is guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 138` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 138(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 138(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
